<title>CANADA: CMHC sets C$400 mln 5.5 percent bond due 2002.</title>
<headline>CMHC sets C$400 mln 5.5 percent bond due 2002.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Mortgage and Housing Corp on Thursday set C$400 million of 5.5 percent bonds due September 3, 2002 in financial markets, lead manager RBC Dominion Securities Inc said.  </p>
<p>The bond was priced at 98.778 to yield 5.773, eight basis points over the Government of Canada's 5.5 percent bond due September, 2002.</p>
<p>The bond will be delivered on June 19 and pays interest on September 3 and March 3.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
